{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>תככים</b> — that poverty has broken him, like מתוך (oppression) and מחמס, and in this sense תוכו לרגליך נשברו, and it would be תכך and תכה." "<b>נפגשו</b> — for the wicked and poverty, when HaShem decrees them and they descend from heaven like rain falling upon the earth, they meet them, and they are נפגשו." "<b>מאיר</b> — for they walk in the darkness of poverty, and HaShem illuminates their eyes to fill their lack, and all is according to deeds." "Another interpretation: <b>תככים</b> — that they robbed his wealth through תוך and deceit."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra quotes partial forms and verses without full citation; מתוך likely refers to Proverbs 30:14 or a similar usage, and תוכו לרגליך נשברו echoes Jeremiah 38:6; rendered hyper-literally as the grammatical argument is elliptical."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:25:25.371639228Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}